<title>SINGAPORE: Avimo half year net profit up 40.35 pct.</title>
<headline>Avimo half year net profit up 40.35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		4.50     vs    3.21</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)	  1.50     vs    1.25</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)     4.31     vs    3.07</p>
<p>    Turnover		 67.77     vs   60.34</p>
<p>    Operating profit	9.68     vs    7.49</p>
<p>    Interest expense	1.22     vs    1.17</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  5.47     vs    3.50</p>
<p>    Associates		0.59     vs    0.67</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.46     vs    0.92</p>
<p>    Minorities	     (0.10)    vs   (0.05)</p>
<p>Dividend pay/register - August 14 1997/ July 29 1997</p>
<p>Note - Aerospace optic and laser systems maker Avimo Group Ltd said growth would be sustained in the second half due to increased capacity from its Singapore optics operations, renewed growth in semiconductor equipment market and an initial contribution from the Apache contract at Avimo Taunton, U.K. Avimo is 38 percent owned by British defence manufacturer Alvis Plc.     -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
